            "author": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "activeRequest is assigned inside the case before the rc check, so on encode failure it stays non-empty and update()'s empty() guard (which only covers the default case) won't skip it.\nSuggest `if (rc == 0) { activeRequest = requestVx; }` so a failed encode leaves it empty and gets skipped."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 174,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "This empty() check only catches the unknown-deviceType (default) case. It won't catch an encode failure, because activeRequest is assigned before the rc check in the ctor (see \uff0346 comment there)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 174,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieInterface.cpp",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Same problem here \u2014 activeRequest is assigned before the rc check in the ctor. Gate it on rc == 0 like the others.\n\nSame pattern in the other three PCIe classes (NvidiaPcieInterface, NvidiaPciePort,\nNvidiaPciePortMetrics) \u2014 same fix applies to each."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieInterface.cpp",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
