        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "88119e18d565f6be51c87aa232b6d13a76b32399",
            "parents": [
                "07bffee9035970b000900a23d50de70ef7a92ddd"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/47/90947/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "createdOn": 1781334393,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "If there is no interchanging case happens, I think we can simply make use of `const std::vector<uint8_t>` to store the encoded requests."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "One interchangable case I can think of is that, the backend device performed firmware update at the daemon runtime.\n\nIn this case, the updated device could have switched to another version.\nHowever, I am not sure if we should also be handling that case here.\n\nIf we are going to handle that case here, obviously checking only `activeRequest.empty()` isn't enough here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Handling runtime version switch would be a separate change (likely tied to MCTP re-discovery). Keeping it out of scope here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.hpp",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do we need to keep both v1 and v2 request but used only one of them at runtime?\nIs there a case where a given instance would possibly sending v1 and v2 request interchangingly?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.hpp",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Good Catch. Done."
                }
            ],
